Consumer Group
A consumer group allows multiple consumers to read data in parallel.
Example:

Topic: transactions
Partitions: 3

Consumer Group: fraud-service

Consumer1 → Partition 0
Consumer2 → Partition 1
Consumer3 → Partition 2
Important rule:
One partition → only one consumer in a group



🔁 Kafka Message Flow

Producer
   ↓
Kafka Topic  (each type of data have a topic)
   ↓
Partitions  (each topic split into smaller parts for parallel processing)
   ↓
Kafka Brokers (Cluster)  A cluster is multiple Kafka brokers working together.
   ↓
Consumer Group   (A consumer group allows multiple consumers to read data in parallel.)


Producer → Topic (partitioned) → Broker → Consumer Group → Consumers
📦 Example of Kafka Topic Structure

Topic: order-events

Partition 0: [offset 0] [offset 1] ...
Partition 1: [offset 0] [offset 1] ...
Each consumer group reads one offset per partition, meaning multiple apps can process the same data independently.

3️⃣ Kafka Replication (Very Important Question)

Kafka replicates data to avoid data loss.\
Example:

Broker1 → Leader
Broker2 → Follower
Broker3 → Follower

Producer writes to Leader partition.
Followers replicate data.
If leader fails → follower becomes leader.
This provides fault tolerance.

